# Security Checklist

## Authentication & Authorization

- [ ] All protected routes have a `CanActivateFn` guard
- [ ] Redirect unauthenticated users to login page
- [ ] Token stored in `sessionStorage` (not `localStorage` — vulnerable to XSS)
- [ ] All API calls attach the token via an HTTP interceptor
- [ ] Handle 401 responses globally — redirect to login
- [ ] Role/permission checks before showing sensitive UI
- [ ] Never trust client-side permissions alone — always validate server-side

## XSS Prevention

- [ ] **Never** use `innerHTML` with user-generated content
- [ ] Use `{{ expression }}` (Angular auto-sanitizes) or `textContent`
- [ ] If HTML must be rendered, use DOMPurify with explicit allowlist
- [ ] Validate and escape all user input before rendering
- [ ] External URLs must be validated before navigation

## External Links

- [ ] All external links have `target="_blank"` with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`
- [ ] Validate URLs start with `http://` or `https://` before use

## Form Security

- [ ] Validate all form inputs (client-side + server-side)
- [ ] Prevent double-submission (disable button while loading)
- [ ] Use Reactive Forms with built-in validators
- [ ] Never trust form data from the client alone

## File Uploads

- [ ] Validate file type on client (MIME check)
- [ ] Validate file size limit before upload
- [ ] Never execute uploaded files on the server
- [ ] Store uploads outside web root

## Data Exposure

- [ ] No sensitive data in URL query parameters
- [ ] No sensitive data in `console.log` or error messages
- [ ] API errors return generic messages to the client — never expose stack traces
- [ ] Sensitive data masked in UI (e.g., password fields)

## HTTP Security

- [ ] All API calls use HTTPS in production
- [ ] CORS configured to allow only known origins
- [ ] API calls go through service layer — never direct HTTP in components
- [ ] Rate limit sensitive operations (debounce, throttle)

## Common Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ Safe — Angular sanitizes by default
<span>{{ userInput }}</span>

// ✅ Safe — external links
<a [href]="safeUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">

// ❌ Dangerous — XSS risk
<div [innerHTML]="userHtml"></div>

// ❌ Dangerous — open redirect
window.location.href = userProvidedUrl;
```

```typescript
// Validate external URL before navigation
function isSafeRedirect(url: string): boolean {
  try {
    const parsed = new URL(url);
    return ['http:', 'https:'].includes(parsed.protocol);
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```
